    "updated_at": "2015-10-07T20:17:23Z",
    "body": "Thanks @Ritsyy! This looks great; just please follow the [guidelines for writing good commit messages](https://github.com/erlang/otp/wiki/Writing-good-commit-messages). That means giving it a nice title. For example, I might do\n\n```\nRemove multicol from elements with default margins\n\nFixes https://www.w3.org/Bugs/Public/show_bug.cgi?id=27672.\n```\n\nYou could also include some detail, like \"Firefox is the only element with default styles for multicol.\" Optional though, since people can just click the link.\n\nIf you could amend your commit to have a message like this, and force-push it to your branch, then I'd be happy to merge it!\n",
